235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The findings of this project highlight the profound and accelerating impact of Artificial Intelligence on the global job market. Through comprehensive analysis, data modeling, and visualization, it becomes evident that AI is not merely influencing isolated tasks, but reshaping entire job categories, required skill sets, and long-term workforce structures.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The integration of AI has already begun automating routine, repetitive, and predictable tasks across various sectors. Jobs that rely heavily on manual, rule-based operations show significantly higher automation risk. However, the results also reveal a parallel trend: while certain roles are declining, AI is simultaneously driving the creation of new technology-oriented and hybrid job opportunities that require advanced analytical, digital, and problem-solving skills.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
